From c9ae994cfb878030855ebe69a56c59771ca6e91d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dzagah Jeremiah <134429752+jayblitz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:39:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Network switch: Monad and Stellar in the internal build
 (build 24)

Home's balance card starts with a network chip ("Monad"). Tapping it opens a sheet that switches to Stellar, and the
app's screens change with the network: Stellar Home, Earn, Launch and Moments from the DyorLite package, with Monad one
tap away. The first switch explains itself, then unlocks, signs in, takes an invite and sets up the Stellar account in
one checklist.

The App Store target stays build 23 apart from the build number. Every change to an existing file sits inside
#if STELLAR_LITE, and the new code is in DyorHQ/Lite/, compiled only by the internal project that Internal/generate.py
makes (DyorHQInternal, with the StellarKit and DyorLite packages from multichain-stellar).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
